    Help { cmd: "refactor table", text: "volec refactor table X [--count X_COUNT] [--cap X_CAP] [--alloc base::comp::Comp]   static var X: *T to Vec<T, Comp>\n\
  X = grow(X, X_COUNT, &X_CAP) goes; X[X_COUNT] = v; ... X_COUNT += 1; is X.push(v); (a read between them: X.len() - 1);\n\
  a read of X_COUNT is X.len(), X_COUNT = 0 X.clear(), X_COUNT -= k X.truncate(X.len() - k); X[i], X[i].f, X[a..b] stay;\n\
  X_COUNT's and X_CAP's statics and imports go. Refused, nothing changed, each use listed: &X[i] (a raw pointer into it),\n\
    X itself passed or assigned, X_CAP read, another write of X_COUNT, a call between a store and its += 1 that reads X_COUNT\n\
  --count, --cap: the statics' names (default: X without its S, or X, then _COUNT, _CAP); --dry-run: the diff;\n\
    then fix --only unneeded-unsafe (the blocks only the raw indexing needed)\n" },
    Help {
        cmd: "refactor inline",
