  --list (PATTERN alone too): a line per site, what its holes matched; --where '$v: name ~ RE' or $v~/RE/: names only\n\
  --subst 'PATTERN' 'REPL': inside the code the holes keep; a hole the pattern lacks is a new name (`for $x in`)\n\
volec rewrite --text OLD NEW [--files GLOB]... --dry-run --diff   text in any file git tracks (0.21), one edit for undo\n\
  --word (no letter or digit around: VOLE_ROOT has VOLE), --case (any case; NEW in the match's), --regex (in a line)\n\
  --comments, --strings, --code: in vole sources only there; --no-sources: the other files; --move-paths: paths too (git mv)\n\
  --exclude GLOB | GLOB:/RE/ (lines) | GLOB:/A/,/B/ (A up to before B), --exclude-from FILE; --check ROOT: no new error\n" },
    Help { cmd: "fix", text: "volec fix   every machine-applicable fix: imports, unused, pub, unsafe\n\
  --suggested: the exact fixes the errors' `try: volec fix --suggested` names (a did-you-mean name with one candidate,\n\
    a conversion, a path from crate::, a Rust spelling, a missing use or pub, a missing `gpa` argument) that keep the meaning (else note fix.refused), one checked edit; prints the errors left\n\
  --only imports,unused,pub,unsafe,suggested,reexports,tidy-imports,std015,unneeded-unsafe; --in FILE|MODULE; --at FILE:LINE;\n\
    --codes CODE,... (the errors' codes: conv.marker,conv.rust); --dry-run, --show, --diff (what was written); --use PATH::NAME (fix.ambiguous)\n\
  (asked for only: unneeded-unsafe, the unsafe blocks with nothing unsafe inside taken away, their code kept in scope;\n\
    unneeded-justified: the justified too, with their comments; std015: 0.14's parse_int, next_int, read_line, read_stdin given .ok(), .unwrap_or(false), .unwrap())\n\
  --values (0.17, or --only values): parameters to references, with every call: *T written through\n\
    -> &mut T (&x -> &mut x), else &T; a written [T] -> &mut [T]; an owned value only read -> &T (v -> &v); defer v.free(); deleted where v drops;\n\
    a raw pointer stays *T: one passed to C, given c\"...\" or null, compared, indexed, cast or stored, and one passed on to it\n\
  --only conventions (0.20, docs/design/conventions.md §9.2): 0.19's spelling to 0.20's, by types: x: &T -> x: T,\n\
    &mut T -> inout T, an owned by-value x: T -> sink T, receivers self / inout self / sink self, &mut v -> &v, &v to a let -> v,\n\
    *r of an access -> r, let mut -> var, let r = &mut v -> inout r = &v, static var, sink ||, fields let T / inout T;\n\
    checked with --syntax=0.20; what needs a decision is reported (fix.conv_left; --list-left: each place)\n\
  --only conventions-spelling: only what Phase 0 means as 0.19 did (x: let T, &v and *r kept): checks and runs as before\n" },
    Help { cmd: "check", text: "volec check [ROOT] [-I DIR]   the front end's errors, one line each (FILE:L:C: error[KIND] MESSAGE | help: ...); none: `ok: 0 errors in ROOT` on stderr (a build: `ok: built PROG`; VOLE_OK=0: nothing); -I DIR: where `import \"header.h\"` looks first, as for a build\n" },
    Help {
        cmd: "fmt",
